{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence efficiently without recursion.\n    The sequence is defined by fib4(0)=0, fib4(1)=0, fib4(2)=2, fib4(3)=0, and fib4(n) = fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4) for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the first four values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iterate from n=4 up to the requested n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next value and update the rolling window\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, a + b + c + d\n    return d"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list cannot be empty\")\n\n    nums = []\n    for x in l:\n        try:\n            nums.append(float(x))\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Non-numeric value in list: {x!r}\")\n\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    mid = n // 2\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For odd length, return the middle element, cast to int for exact integer results as per example.\n        return int(nums[mid])\n    else:\n        # For even length, return the average of the two middle elements.\n        return (nums[mid - 1] + nums[mid]) / 2.0"}
